{"type":"route","meta":{"status":200,"headers":{"cache-control":"public, max-age=3600","content-type":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8","x-robots-tag":"noindex","x-next-cache-tags":"_N_T_/layout,_N_T_/md/layout,_N_T_/md/[...slug]/layout,_N_T_/md/[...slug]/route,_N_T_/md/roadmap"}},"body":"# Roadmap\n\n> What we are building next for Amantrika, roughly in order — written as intentions rather than promises, with dates deliberately left off.\n\n- Source: http://localhost:3000/roadmap\n- Last updated: 8 August 2026\n\n---\nThis is what we intend to build next, roughly in order. There are no dates: a\ndate given to a customer is a promise, and we would rather keep the promises we\nmake on the [changelog](/changelog), where everything listed already works.\n\n### Nothing on this page works yet\n\nIf something here is important to your wedding, plan as though it will not\nexist. Everything that does exist is on the [changelog](/changelog).\n\n## Next\n\nThe things we are actively working on.\n\n### In progress: Real payments\n\nCard, UPI and netbanking through a payment provider, replacing the demo checkout.\nInvoices, refunds, and partner commissions paid out on a schedule rather than\ntracked on a ledger.\n\n### In progress: Faster invitations\n\nPages should open instantly on a mid-range phone over patchy mobile data,\nbecause that is what most of your guests are using. Caching what rarely changes,\nloading photographs more intelligently, and reducing what has to be fetched\nbefore the first paint.\n\n### Next: Guest messaging\n\nSend the invitation from Amantrika itself instead of copying links by hand.\nPersonalised links per guest, delivery and open tracking, and reminders to the\npeople who have not yet replied — without turning into something that spams your\nrelatives.\n\n## Soon after\n\n### Planned: Your invitation in your language\n\nHindi, Gujarati, Marathi, Tamil, Telugu, Kannada, Bengali, Punjabi, Malayalam,\nOdia and Urdu — with a machine-drafted first pass you review and correct, proper\ntransliteration for names, and script-aware fonts.\n\nAn elder reading the invitation in the language they think in is worth more than\nalmost any feature on this list.\n\n### Planned: Your own domain\n\nPoint a domain you own at your invitation, so the link you share on WhatsApp is\nentirely yours.\n\n### Planned: After the wedding\n\nAn invitation should not stop being useful once the day is over. A private album\nyour guests can add their own photographs to, and an archive page the invitation\ngracefully becomes rather than simply expiring.\n\n### Planned: More occasions, more traditions\n\nMore themes, and more traditions represented properly rather than recoloured —\neach with its own motifs, vocabulary and ceremonies.\n\n## Under consideration\n\nIdeas we think are good but have not committed to. Tell us if one of these is\nthe thing standing between you and a finished invitation.\n\n  <IconCard icon=\"mandap\" title=\"Seating and tables\">Arrange tables, assign guests, and let each guest find their own seat from their personalised link.</IconCard>\n  <IconCard icon=\"AcrossOceans\" title=\"Livestream\">A built-in place for relatives who cannot travel to watch the ceremony.</IconCard>\n  <IconCard icon=\"mithai\" title=\"Gift registry\">A registry, and a cleaner way to receive blessings as gifts than posting a UPI ID.</IconCard>\n  <IconCard icon=\"invitation-scroll\" title=\"Printed cards\">Order matching printed cards from the invitation you have already designed, for the people you visit in person.</IconCard>\n\n## What we will not do\n\nWorth saying plainly, because the absence of these is a decision rather than an\noversight.\n\n  <IconCard icon=\"KeptPrivate\" title=\"Sell or share your guest list\">Your guests' names and numbers are yours. They are never sold, shared, or used to advertise anything.</IconCard>\n  <IconCard icon=\"CardToLink\" title=\"Require an app\">Guests open a link in the browser they already have. No download, no login, no OTP — ever.</IconCard>\n  <IconCard icon=\"nazar\" title=\"Put ads on your invitation\">Your invitation will never carry advertising for us or anybody else.</IconCard>\n  <IconCard icon=\"GuidingLamp\" title=\"Take your invitation down without warning\">If anything ever has to change about how long invitations stay up, you will hear it from us directly and well in advance.</IconCard>\n\n---\n\nMissing something? [Tell us](/contact) — what couples and planners actually run\ninto shapes this list far more than our own guesses do.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### Are these dates guaranteed?\n\nThere are no dates on this page, deliberately. Software estimates given to customers are usually wrong, and a missed date is worse than no date. Items are ordered by what we intend to build next, and things move.\n\n### Can I ask for something that is not listed?\n\nYes, and it is the most useful message you can send us. What gets built next is shaped far more by what couples and planners actually run into than by anything on this page.\n\n### What has already shipped?\n\nThe changelog lists everything that is live today. Nothing on the roadmap works yet — if it did, it would have moved to the changelog.\n"}